Title:
mockdr — Multi-EDR Mock Server

Type:
GitHub Tool

Short Summary (4-8 sentences max):
mockdr is a self-contained mock server that emulates eight security platforms’ APIs (SentinelOne, CrowdStrike Falcon, Microsoft Defender for Endpoint, Elastic Security/Kibana, Cortex XDR, Splunk SIEM, Microsoft Sentinel, and Microsoft Graph). It solves the problem of testing SOAR playbooks, SIEM connectors, and automation scripts without needing real tenants, licenses, VPN access, or dealing with rate limits—while keeping realistic request/response envelopes, auth flows, and query semantics. The project emphasizes “measured fidelity” via conformance tooling that compares mock responses against real products or published specs, plus seeded datasets so tests validate answers (not just JSON shapes). It includes functional query engines for Splunk SPL and MDE/Graph/Sentinel KQL-like hunting, deterministic seed data, scenario triggers (infection waves, compliance drift, risky sign-ins), fault injection, and a recording proxy to capture/replay real vendor exchanges. Useful for red teams/pentesters validating EDR-response tooling pre-engagement, and for blue teams/SOAR/SIEM engineers building and regression-testing integrations. Interesting because it models multiple vendors in one process with realistic auth, pagination, headers, and query behavior—reducing integration brittleness and improving CI reliability.

Technical Focus:
- Multi-vendor API emulation (EDR/SIEM/SOAR) with real paths and response envelopes  
- Auth flows: ApiToken, OAuth2 client credentials, Basic/API Key, Splunk session/HEC, Cortex XDR digest auth  
- Conformance testing against real products/specs (schema/field drift, seeded answer comparison)  
- Query engines: Splunk SPL execution, KQL/Advanced Hunting evaluation, OData/FQL parsing  
- Recording proxy (record/replay) for deterministic fixtures and offline testing  
- Scenario engine, fault injection, rate limiting, and request auditing/metrics (ASGI middleware)

Use Cases:
- Validate SOAR playbooks across multiple EDRs without live tenants
- Regression-test SIEM ingestion/parsers and field mappings with deterministic datasets
- Develop and CI-test vendor SDK-based automation (Python/Go/PowerShell) offline
- Pre-flight red team EDR interaction tooling (contain/isolate, IOC ops, alert triage workflows)
- Capture real API traffic via proxy to build replayable fixtures for integration tests

Keywords:
SentinelOne, CrowdStrike Falcon, Microsoft Defender for Endpoint, Elastic Security, Kibana, Cortex XDR, Splunk SIEM, Microsoft Sentinel, Microsoft Graph API, FastAPI, ASGI middleware, OAuth2 client credentials, OData v4, KQL, Advanced Hunting, SPL, HEC token, API mocking, record/replay proxy, conformance testing